course: dictionary
lesson: 10153
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word thrown is a form of «throw», so it tells you something was sent through the air from a hand. «Fireworks and firecrackers thrown at people or houses can cause burns, fires and great fright.» Here thrown means hurled, sent flying toward a target.
explain: The same word can mean other things. Thrown away means put in the bin as rubbish, and «the question threw me» means the question confused or surprised me. Thrown from a bike means made to fall off it.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around thrown. Ask: is something flying through the air, being binned, or leaving someone puzzled? Then put your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: «Thrown» is a form of the verb «throw»: throw, throws, threw, thrown, throwing.
fact: Something thrown has been sent through the air from the hand.
fact: «Thrown away» means put in the bin as rubbish.
fact: «The question threw me» means the question confused or surprised me, and «thrown from a horse» means made to fall off it.
fact: Thrown-away rubbish should be recycled, so think before you throw things away.
exercise: The ball was thrown high over the fence. What does thrown mean here? | Confused or surprised | Made to fall off | Put in the bin as rubbish | *Sent through the air from the hand
exercise: The old bag was thrown away after it tore. What does thrown away mean? | Taken off the bike | *Put in the bin as rubbish | Sent through the air to a friend | Made to fall off a horse
exercise: Find and copy the word that is a form of «throw» in this sentence: «The fireworks were thrown at the wall.» | wall | at | *thrown | fireworks
test: «The question threw me, so I had to read it twice.» What does threw me mean here? | Hit me with a ball | *Confused me | Let me go early | Made me laugh
test: Which phrase means put in the bin as rubbish? | Thrown on | Thrown from | Thrown in | *Thrown away
exam: «Fireworks and firecrackers thrown at people or houses can cause burns, fires and great fright.» In this sentence, thrown means | Made to fall off a bike | Confused or surprised | *Sent or hurled through the air from the hand | Taken away and recycled
